<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kekaulike</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1736</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kekaulike was ruler (aliʻi nui) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a> in the early 18th century, who died around 1736. He strengthened royal power, built temples and invaded the island of Hawaiʻi, raiding the Kona coast, but was driven back. His sons included Kamehamehanui and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahekili-ii">Kahekili II</a>, who succeeded him in turn and made Maui a leading power of the islands.</p></div>
